<title>FRANCE: PSA Peugeot nine month sales up 6.9 pct.</title>
<headline>PSA Peugeot nine month sales up 6.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover				     130,095    vs  121,687</p>
<p>     - Cars					123,284    vs  114,902</p>
<p>	 Automobiles Peugeot		    73,567    vs   67,279</p>
<p>	 Automobiles Citroen		    49,584    vs   47,422</p>
<p>	 Other					   133    vs	201</p>
<p>     - Mechanical activities, services     6,808    vs    6,782</p>
<p>     - Holding company activities		  3    vs	  3</p>
<p>NOTE - PSA Peugeot Citroen said in a statement that sales rose 6.9 percent in the first nine months of 1996 and 16.5 percent in the third quarter.</p>
<p>Its nine-month sales in France rose 7.4 percent to 58.53 billion francs and 6.5 percent abroad to 71.57 billion.</p>
<p>In unit terms, total nine-month sales rose to 1.49 million vehicles from 1.38 million, up 8.2 percent.</p>
<p>The group's share of the European car market over the nine-month period was 12.02 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
